WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.617
This video shows how to run a SWAT+ model
that you built yourself,

00:00:04.617 --> 00:00:06.990
and what SWATrust does with its folder.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:14.700
This video uses a copy of the basin
02070002, North Branch Potomac.

00:00:14.900 --> 00:00:22.030
The copy lies in the folder my_basin, and
its file time.sim runs from 2005 to 2014.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.910
It stands in for your own model.

00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:27.589
A model folder is a folder that holds the
file

00:00:27.589 --> 00:00:30.560
file.cio and the input files that it
names.

00:00:30.760 --> 00:00:32.610
It is often named TxtInOut.

00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:35.050
In Set-up, click Clear choice.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:37.430
No model of the list is chosen now.

00:00:40.126 --> 00:00:41.646
Click Add a model folder.

00:00:43.638 --> 00:00:46.248
Go to the folder of your model, here
my_basin.

00:00:46.448 --> 00:00:51.748
For a model, the dialog says: This folder
is a model, it holds file.cio.

00:00:55.459 --> 00:00:56.729
Click Add this folder.

00:00:59.457 --> 00:01:04.534
The model is now in the list Models under
the name of its folder,

00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:10.237
with its number of HRUs and the years of
its file time.sim, 2005 to 2014.

00:01:10.437 --> 00:01:15.147
It is the only model chosen, and the line
beside the heading ends 1 chosen.

00:01:15.649 --> 00:01:20.278
The three boxes of the period hold the
years of your model:

00:01:20.278 --> 00:01:23.259
2005, 2014 and its warm-up of 3 years.

00:01:23.761 --> 00:01:27.261
For a folder that holds no model, the
dialog says:

00:01:27.261 --> 00:01:31.041
No model in this folder or in the two
levels below it:

00:01:31.041 --> 00:01:33.141
a model folder holds file.cio.

00:01:33.643 --> 00:01:35.618
Add this folder then adds nothing,

00:01:35.618 --> 00:01:39.683
and the page repeats the sentence under
the button Add a model folder.

00:01:43.241 --> 00:01:44.621
Click Continue to Run.

00:01:44.821 --> 00:01:50.721
The table lists the model with its years,
2005 to 2014, and its warm-up, 3.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:58.660
Click Start the run, and wait until the
page reads: 1 of 1 basin finished.

00:02:16.207 --> 00:02:17.437
Click See the results.

00:02:17.637 --> 00:02:19.488
Beside the heading Results,

00:02:19.488 --> 00:02:24.424
the page gives the years that the run
wrote to its tables, 2008 to 2014:

00:02:24.424 --> 00:02:29.907
the first three years are the warm-up,
simulated, but not written to the tables.

00:02:33.304 --> 00:02:36.034
A run does not write to the folder of your
model.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:38.920
Each run gets a new folder in the runs
folder,

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:42.424
with a copy of the model and the tables
that the run writes.

00:02:42.926 --> 00:02:47.606
The next chapter, Run streamflow, runs a
basin and reads the flow at its outlet.
